# Machine-checked rounding-error bound for relay-math's f32 sin polynomial
# (MATHF32-P03, the proof track for MATHF32-P01/P02 — rules_rocq_rust#37/#41).
#
# CLAIM (rounding-error LAYER only): over the reduced range r in [-0.8, 0.8]
# — the interval the Cody-Waite reduction clamps to, containing [-pi/4,pi/4]
# — the f32 Horner evaluation of sin_poly differs from the EXACT real value
# of the SAME polynomial (same f32 coefficients, no rounding) by at most
# 2^-24 (one ULP at unit magnitude — the tight machine-checked bound:
# coqc accepts 2^-24, rejects 2^-25). I.e. the floating-point evaluation is faithful to the mathematics
# it implements. This is one of the two ingredients behind the exhaustive
# 1.19e-7 absolute-error bound (MATHF32-P02); the OTHER — that this
# polynomial approximates the true sine (the minimax remainder |P(r)-sin r|)
# — is the Coq-Interval layer, tracked separately, NOT proven here.
#
# `gappa -Bcoq` emits a Flocq/Rocq proof term; gappa_proof (rules_rocq_rust)
# kernel-checks it with coqc — Gappa's own success is never trusted (CC-002).
#
# Kernel source: crates/relay-math/src/lib.rs, sin_poly():
#   z = r*r;  r + r*z*(S1 + z*(S2 + z*S3))
# evaluated left-to-right in f32 (each op rounds to nearest-even).

@rnd = float<ieee_32,ne>;

# Exact f32 coefficients (bit-identical to the compiled constants).
S1 = -0x1.5555460p-3;
S2 =  0x1.11073c0p-7;
S3 = -0x1.9943f20p-13;

# r is a float in the reduced range.
r = rnd(rin);

# --- f32 evaluation, operation-for-operation with the kernel ---
z  rnd= r * r;
t0 rnd= z * S3;
t1 rnd= S2 + t0;
t2 rnd= z * t1;
t3 rnd= S1 + t2;      # inner = S1 + z*(S2 + z*S3)
rz rnd= r * z;
pr rnd= rz * t3;      # r*z*inner
Msin rnd= r + pr;

# --- exact real value of the SAME polynomial (same coefficients) ---
Ez  = r * r;
Et0 = Ez * S3;
Et1 = S2 + Et0;
Et2 = Ez * Et1;
Et3 = S1 + Et2;
Erz = r * Ez;
Epr = Erz * Et3;
Esin = r + Epr;

{ rin in [-0.8, 0.8] -> |Msin - Esin| <= 1b-24 }
